    "methodology": "10,000-game solitaire heuristic. Sequencing: land drop, cheapest ramp, commander on affordability, biggest affordable threat, then other proactive spells. Meaningful board = pressure score >= 7 or 2+ threats. Lethal proxy = cumulative combat-pressure proxy >= 40; combat pressure uses mana-value-based creature scoring because card metadata omits power/toughness. Combo lethal = at least one winConditions[] entry tagged kind:'combo' has all pieces present (hand, battlefield, or substitutable) and combined mana cost payable. Substitution priority for missing pieces: (1) bargain free-cast tutor (e.g. Beseech the Mirror) when a non-rock enchantment is on battlefield OR commander has been in play for 1+ turn (approximates Sauron-style amass token from real-game opponent casts); (2) type-matched regular tutor whose tutor_targets includes piece's card type and tutor_mv_cap permits piece's MV; (3) reanimation spell (decklist[].primary_role/secondary_role == 'recursion') for permanent pieces only \u2014 cost replaces piece's cast cost (treats piece as if in graveyard). Each substitute is consumed once per combo line. Tutors, non-permanent combo pieces, and reanimation spells are reserved from filler casting. v2 limitations: no literal graveyard tracking (reanim assumes piece could be in GY), no opponent interaction, no multi-turn assembly tracking, no stack-trigger ordering. Commander transform/free-deploy engine modeled (DEC-405): once the commander is in play, the transform activation (4 generic + colored pips; 2 generic with Training Grounds on the battlefield) is paid on affordability like any other cast. From the transform turn (haste) the 5-power back face attacks every turn, and one artifact from hand is put onto the battlefield free at each combat \u2014 deployed creatures are summoning-sick, deployed kill-piece Equipment (8 configured) add their attach bonus to commander damage, and double-strike Equipment double it. Configured Equipment are held in hand as deploy fuel (no equip-cost path exists in the sim). Floors: the front-face artifact dig, Nexus of Becoming's second deploy stream, backup attachers, and paid equips are not modeled."
